Subject: [PATCH] venus: allocate from a small device-local heap synchronously

vn_device_memory_alloc_simple() submits vkAllocateMemory asynchronously
and reports VK_SUCCESS. When the host allocation fails, the guest never
learns it: the host creates no VkDeviceMemory, and the next command that
names the memory (vkBindBufferMemory2) fails to decode ("failed to look
up object N of type 8"). That is fatal to the whole Venus context, and the
application crashes later (compat finding F4: Unigine Heaven and Valley
with OpenGL on an RTX 5090, an access violation in viogpu_wgl.dll).

The heap that runs out is the small device-local heap of a discrete GPU
without resizable BAR: 246 MiB on an RTX 5090, the host card's BAR1, which
every process and VM on the card shares. Patch 0070 (nvva) stops the guest
from treating it as host-visible, which keeps Zink's streaming buffers out
of it. Memory of that heap can still be allocated as device-local, and the
host still has to back it with BAR1, so an allocation there can still
fail. Drivers expect that and fall back to another heap (Zink, DXVK and
vkd3d-proton all do), but only if they see the error.

Allocate from a device-local heap that is smaller than the largest
device-local heap synchronously, so that the caller sees the host's
result. Where there is one device-local heap (AMD APUs, Intel) or the
visible heap is all of VRAM (resizable BAR), nothing changes.

Applies after 0070 and 0071 (nvva) and does not touch their code.
Evidence: docs/unigl.md, docs/evidence/unigl/.
Origin: vmlab-win3d unigl worker.
---
diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_device_memory.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_device_memory.c
index 5487eb2..a479b46 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_device_memory.c
@@ -28,6 +28,34 @@
 
 /* device memory commands */
 
+/* Whether the memory type is in a small device-local heap: one smaller than
+ * the largest device-local heap, such as the 256 MiB BAR window of a
+ * discrete GPU without resizable BAR. Such a heap runs out in normal use
+ * (on the host every process and VM on the card shares it), and the caller
+ * must see that: Zink, DXVK and vkd3d-proton fall back to another heap on
+ * VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY. An asynchronous allocation reports success
+ * instead, and the next command that names the memory fails to decode on
+ * the host, which is fatal to the whole context.
+ */
+static bool
+vn_device_memory_type_in_small_heap(const struct vn_device *dev,
+                                    uint32_t mem_type_index)
+{
+   const VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties *props =
+      &dev->physical_device->memory_properties;
+   const VkMemoryHeap *heap =
+      &props->memoryHeaps[props->memoryTypes[mem_type_index].heapIndex];
+   if (!(heap->flags & VK_MEMORY_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT))
+      return false;
+
+   for (uint32_t i = 0; i < props->memoryHeapCount; i++) {
+      if ((props->memoryHeaps[i].flags & VK_MEMORY_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT) &&
+          props->memoryHeaps[i].size > heap->size)
+         return true;
+   }
+   return false;
+}
+
 static inline VkResult
 vn_device_memory_alloc_simple(struct vn_device *dev,
                               struct vn_device_memory *mem,
@@ -35,7 +63,8 @@ vn_device_memory_alloc_simple(struct vn_device *dev,
 {
    VkDevice dev_handle = vn_device_to_handle(dev);
    VkDeviceMemory mem_handle = vn_device_memory_to_handle(mem);
-   if (VN_PERF(NO_ASYNC_MEM_ALLOC)) {
+   if (VN_PERF(NO_ASYNC_MEM_ALLOC) ||
+       vn_device_memory_type_in_small_heap(dev, alloc_info->memoryTypeIndex)) {
       return vn_call_vkAllocateMemory(dev->primary_ring, dev_handle,
                                       alloc_info, NULL, &mem_handle);
    }
